<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      The `benchmark` variant only. Not merged into debug and not into release.

      This declares the same seeder as src/debug, with one difference:
      android:exported="true".

      The reason is mechanical rather than a preference. The benchmark variant
      is deliberately **not debuggable** — a debuggable build disables
      optimisations wholesale, so an NFR-PERF number taken on one says nothing
      about what ships. But `am broadcast` from the shell reaches an unexported
      receiver only in a debuggable package, so the same receiver that works in
      debug is unreachable here. Exporting it is what makes the corpus seedable
      on the build the targets are actually defined against.

      What that costs: any app on the device could broadcast this and rewrite
      the ledger. Acceptable, and only here — this variant is a measuring
      instrument that is never published, carries a `.benchmark` application id
      so it cannot replace a real install, and is signed with the debug key.
      `release` has neither this manifest nor the class it names.
    -->
    <application>

        <receiver
            android:name="com.app.finance.dev.SeedReceiver"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="com.app.finance.SEED" />
            </intent-filter>
        </receiver>

    </application>

</manifest>
